The '''PYRAMID30 Okaiken''' is a chart that ranks the best-performing singles in [[Okaiken]]. Its data, published by Nikkan Sports & Entertainment magazine, KTK Group and compiled by Okaiken Pyramid Records, is based collectively on each single's weekly physical and digital sales, as well as radio airplay and streaming. PYRAMID30 Okaiken is a subsidiary of Pyramid Records but acts as a separate organization. The weekly charts are updated every Sunday at 11:45 in the morning (UTC +9). The following lists all of the number one singles of the PYRAMID30 Okaiken for 2019.

2019 marked a pivotal transition in the Okaiken music scene. The dominance of traditional J-Pop and idol groups, which had defined the charts for decades (exemplified by the 2017 chart), began to wane. In their place, a wave of "City Pop Revival" and "Lo-Fi Hip Hop" acts surged to popularity, driven by streaming platforms. Artists like [[Suchmos]] and [[Nulbarich]] bridged the gap between rock and soul, while [[King Gnu]] emerged as the leaders of the new "Tokyo Chaotic" sound, setting the stage for the experimental explosion of 2020. This year is often cited by critics as the "Twilight of the Idol Era" and the dawn of the "Artist Era."

